# Version bump (main)

Canonical: one line in `VERSION`, mirrored in `project.godot` → `application/config/version`. The HUD and main menu read that setting (`v0.1.0-alpha`). Keep the `-alpha` suffix until the user asks to drop it or cut a named release.

## When to bump

When the user asks to **commit**, **merge**, or **open a PR** that will land **code** on `main`, bump in that same commit (or as the last commit before merge):

```
python dev/bump_version.py patch
# or: python dev/bump_version.py minor
```

Stage `VERSION` + `project.godot`. Still wait for an explicit commit/push ask.

Do **not** bump for docs-only / comments / `.cursor/` / changelog-only work, feature-branch commits that are not merging to `main`, a commit that already changed `VERSION`, or when the message contains `[skip bump]`.

CI (`.github/workflows/bump-version.yml`) patch-bumps on push to `main` if code landed and `VERSION` was not already updated.

## Which number

- **patch** (default): fixes, polish, small tweaks
- **minor**: new player-facing feature; also pre-1.0 breaking changes
- **major**: only after 1.0, or when the user asks

Do **not** freeze `[Unreleased]` into a dated changelog section on auto-bumps. Only do that when the user asks to **release**.
